we have called Data Bytes.

00:50:27.630 --> 00:50:30.180
And basically what it is
is either bringing somebody from

00:50:30.180 --> 00:50:33.060
IT or somebody from the
community to talk about the

00:50:33.060 --> 00:50:35.370
work that they're doing and/or--

00:50:35.370 --> 00:50:35.910
more recently,

00:50:35.910 --> 00:50:39.510
we had one that was
actually somebody that participated in

00:50:39.510 --> 00:50:43.170
Data Jam and wanted to leverage
the Data Jam network to look at

00:50:43.170 --> 00:50:44.895
their data and help
generate insights.

00:50:45.840 --> 00:50:47.610
And I know we've
also talked about

00:50:48.510 --> 00:50:51.000
doing some more collective

00:50:51.810 --> 00:50:53.770
meetings across the
different communities,

00:50:53.770 --> 00:50:56.310
so gathering all the different
communities together on a more

00:50:56.310 --> 00:50:58.830
regular basis because data
Jam did bring a lot of those

00:50:58.830 --> 00:50:59.670
communities together.

00:51:00.700 --> 00:51:03.360
And so there are definitely
plans to start it,

00:51:03.360 --> 00:51:04.590
to continue that.

00:51:04.590 --> 00:51:06.710
It's been a little bit
hectic at Biogen lately,

00:51:06.710 --> 00:51:09.340
so we haven't been able to do as
much as we wanted to. But I think

00:51:10.150 --> 00:51:12.010
now that things are
somewhat settling,

00:51:12.010 --> 00:51:15.415
we are definitely looking
at the next few key events.

00:51:16.330 --> 00:51:18.810
ALAN: Well, thanks. I
hope those are successful.

00:51:18.810 --> 00:51:21.010
It sounds like a
really good foundation.

00:51:21.010 --> 00:51:23.950
